  "body": "Second slice of #1449. This PR does not close the issue: see \"Not exercised\".\n\n## What changed\n\n- The 2D Pocket page has a new group, \"Entry positions (pre-drilled)\", on the `Lead in / Lead out` tab. It is below \"Horizontal arc entry\".\n- The group has one header switch. The switch writes `links.approach.predrilled` into the page draft.\n- Apply commits the draft through `EditOperationParams`. Undo and redo restore the flag.\n- The open group shows one line. The line says where the holes come from, when a hole is used, and that each other level keeps the asked entry.\n- When rest machining is on in the draft, the group also shows `REST_PREDRILLED`. That is the refusal that Apply gives.\n- The pages of the other kinds do not show the group. Those kinds refuse the flag (`PREDRILLED_POCKET_ONLY`).\n\nFiles:\n\n- `crates/ui/src/egui_app/predrilled_page.rs` (new, 34 lines): the group.\n- `crates/ui/src/egui_app/predrilled_page_tests.rs` (new): the structural tests.\n- `crates/ui/src/egui_app/mill2d_page.rs`: one call in the Pocket arm (398 lines now).\n- `crates/ui/src/egui_app/mod.rs`: two `mod` lines.\n- `docs/decisions/1449-predrilled-entry-group.md`: the decision entry.\n\n## Cause\n\nSlice 1 (#1493) added the flag for MCP and for project files only. The page had no control for it. The issue comment of 2026-11-13 lists the UI group and its structural test as owed.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\nAll three tests are in `camcraft-ui`, under `egui_app::predrilled_page_tests`:\n\n- `the_pre_drilled_group_is_on_the_pocket_lead_tab_only_and_off_by_default`\n- `the_pre_drilled_group_switch_edits_the_draft_and_apply_commits_an_undoable_edit`\n- `the_pre_drilled_group_names_the_refusal_beside_rest_machining`\n\nFinal code head: `9dd166f05df1c4cebfd1255c43bda69ecfb2c50c`.\n\n## Review fixes\n\nThe test fixtures now set `corner_relief: Default::default()`, `pass_start: Default::default()`, and `source: RestSource::EnteredTool`. These values keep relief and a custom start off. The rest fixture uses the entered tool dimensions.\n\nThe branch includes `upstream/main` at `35940da16955dd450eccf9a7bc61471f7f6cdafa` through a clean merge. The final quick and heavy gates used current `upstream/main` at `74ea8988d800f00d41547ec9d292077d2bc3ddc5`. The later base commit changes the Mach3 post only.\n\n## Pin proof\n\nCommand: `RUSTC_WRAPPER=sccache cargo test -j 6 -p camcraft-ui --lib predrilled_page_tests`.\n\nBefore the fixture fix: RED. The compiler reports E0063 for missing `corner_relief`, `pass_start`, and `source`.\n\nAfter the fixture fix: GREEN. All three predrilled group tests pass.\n\nThe existing pins cover the group location and default, the draft switch and undoable Apply, and the rest refusal. Each field was removed separately. Each mutation failed with E0063. All three pins passed after restoration.\n\n## Final-head validation\n\n- `CAMCRAFT_GATE_JOBS=6 cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: GREEN. 10 steps, 0 failed. The full UI library suite passed: 1479 passed, 8 ignored. The eight UI integration suites also passed.\n- UI library tests ran in the quick gate, as shown above.\n- `CARGO_INCREMENTAL=0 RUSTC_WRAPPER=sccache cargo clippy -j 6 -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: GREEN.\n- `CAMCRAFT_GATE_JOBS=6 cargo xtask gate heavy --base upstream/main`: GREEN. 0 steps, 0 failed. The diff reaches no heavy lane.\n- `CARGO_INCREMENTAL=0 RUSTC_WRAPPER=sccache cargo test -j 6 -p camcraft-app --test example_catalog`: GREEN. 37 passed, 4 ignored, 0 failed.\n\n## Screenshots\n\nThe images show the actual Pocket `Lead in / Lead out` property page, rendered by the egui kittest harness. No desktop window was opened. The before capture uses the same fixture with only the added group call removed. The after capture enables the new group and shows its contents.\n\n![Before: Pocket lead tab](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/03edacff2d61c113551f31c9e40168f044e578c3/pr-2817/pocket-lead-before.png)\n![After: enabled pre-drilled entry group](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/03edacff2d61c113551f31c9e40168f044e578c3/pr-2817/pocket-lead-after.png)\n\nThe capture code and images are outside the PR tree. The PNG files are stored only on the fork's `pr-screenshots` branch.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. The example catalog suite passed. No recorded programs or snapshot files change in this PR. No golden suite is reached by the UI-only diff.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No desktop window was opened. The UI checks and evidence use the kittest harness.\n- The release pixel snapshot suite did not run. No snapshot PNG changes.\n- No toolpath was generated through the new switch. The generator tests from #1493 cover the parameter.\n\n\nStill owed on #1449 after this PR:\n\n- 2D Adaptive, Slot and the 3D roughing kinds.\n- Holes in the model, typed points with the explicit \"the hole exists\" choice, carried stock from a previous setup.\n- The \"pre-drilled only\" mode.\n- Tools that are not centre-cutting down a hole.\n- A user-set clearance.\n- A golden CL file.\n- The setup-sheet line.\n\n## Overlaps\n\n- No open PR changes `mill2d_page.rs`.\n- #2663, #2714, #2763, #2764 and #2773 change `crates/ui/src/egui_app/mod.rs`. This PR adds two `mod` lines there and changes no function. Whichever merges second refreshes.\n\nMCP: no new command. The flag already has its MCP parameter from #1493.\n\nChangelog: 2D Pocket: the \"Entry positions (pre-drilled)\" group on the Lead in / Lead out tab switches pre-drilled entry on and off from the page (#1449).\n\nEffort: high\n\nRefs #1449\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n",
